---
title: Crash Hot Potatoes
servings: 4
course: Side
prep time: 10m
cook time: 1h
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: Australian
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- side-dish
- australian
- savoury
---

Scrub the @potatoes{700%g} clean and place in a #large saucepan{}. Add enough cold water to cover by about an inch, plus @salt{2%tbsp}. Bring to a boil. Reduce the heat and simmer until the potatoes are very tender and can be easily pierced with a sharp knife with no resistance:\
• Micro potatoes:     7 to ~{10%minutes}\
• Baby red potatoes: 12 to ~{17%minutes}\
• Baby Yukon gold:   20 to ~{25%minutes}\
• Red potatoes:      25 to ~{30%minutes}\
• Yukon gold:        30 to ~{35%minutes}

Drain the potatoes and leave in the saucepan to dry and cool.

> The boiled potatoes can be refrigerated for up to 2 days before roasting.

Preheat oven to 200°C.

Drizzle a #baking sheet{} with @olive oil{2%tbsp} and add the boiled potatoes. Turn the potatoes (or shake the tray) to coat them in the oil. Using the bottom of a lightly greased drinking glass or similar, press down on each potato until it splits open and is flattened to ¾ to 1 inch thick, depending on the size of potato.

Drizzle the potatoes with the remaining @olive oil{1%tbsp}. Season with @salt and @black pepper{}(freshly ground). Optionally add any other flavourings, e.g. @?garlic{}(minced) or @?cheese{}(grated).

Roast at 200°C for about ~{10%minutes} until the bottoms are golden-brown. Increase oven temperature to 275°C and roast for a further 10 to ~{15%minutes} until the tops are brown and crispy.

Serve warm, sprinkled with @?parsley leaves{}(finely chopped) if desired.

> Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.